  "question": {
    "text": "Water flows in a horizontal pipe whose one end is closed with a valve. The reading of the pressure gauge attached to the pipe is $P_1$. The reading of the pressure gauge falls to $P_2$ when the valve is opened. The speed of water flowing in the pipe is proportional to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "t5weN",
      "text": "$P_1-P_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OWz2R",
      "text": "$\\left(P_1-P_2\\right)^4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8rdjZ",
      "text": "$\\left(\\mathrm{P}_1-\\mathrm{P}_2\\right)^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lSJRb",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\mathrm{P}_1-\\mathrm{P}_2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/SQEvWgsWWpMrMAvqbs2IZH5JQqKk9H53py7WCaswVgE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nUsing Bernoulli's theorem\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& P_1-P_2=\\frac{1}{2} \\rho v^2 \\\\\n& v \\propto \\sqrt{P_1-P_2}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
